{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_domsyncgl", "label": "domSyncGL (library overview)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lines 1-18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_webgpu_first_webgl2_fallback", "label": "WebGPU first / WebGL 2 fallback", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Concepts > WebGPU first", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shaders are written as TSL node factories rather than GLSL strings so three can transpile to WGSL or GLSL automatically - the consumer writes one implementation for both backends. WebGPU device acquisition is async, hence the ready Promise."}, {"id": "readme_tsl_node_factory", "label": "TSL node factory shaders", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Concepts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_dom_locked_plane", "label": "DOM-locked plane", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Concepts > DOM-locked plane", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_scroll_sync", "label": "Scroll sync (effective scrollY)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Concepts > Scroll sync", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Effective scrollY comes from -document.documentElement.getBoundingClientRect().top rather than window.scrollY so that iOS Safari rubber-band / pull-to-refresh offsets are captured; feeding the same value to both the container transform and the plane positions keeps canvas and DOM visually aligned without killing pull-to-refresh."}, {"id": "readme_single_raf_loop", "label": "Single rAF loop (Lenis integration)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Concepts > smooth scroll", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two separate rAF loops run in registration order, so if Core registers first it reads a one-frame-stale scrollY and the background canvas drifts while scrolling. Driving lenis.raf() then app.tick() from one loop guarantees ordering. The old rafScroll option / RafScroll class / getRafScroll() were removed as part of this."}, {"id": "readme_dom_text_plane_concept", "label": "DOM text plane (README)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Concepts > DOM text plane", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_post_effects", "label": "Post effects (ping-pong chain)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Concepts > Post effects", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_peer_dependency_policy", "label": "Peer dependency / bundle policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "Bundle", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "three (>= 0.178.0), lil-gui and stats.js are peer dependencies and Lenis is not a runtime dependency at all - smooth scrolling is treated as an app concern; sideEffects: false keeps tree-shaking working."}, {"id": "readme_exports", "label": "Public exports surface", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "API reference > Exports", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_domsyncgl", "target": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_domsyncgl", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "API reference", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_domsyncgl", "target": "readme_webgpu_first_webgl2_fallback", "relation